.TH WEACT-LIST 1 "October 2026" "WeAct Display Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weact-list \- list WeAct USB displays without opening serial ports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weact-list
.RB [ --verbose | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads Linux sysfs tty metadata and resolves existing /dev/serial/by-id links.
Models are selected by Product for VID:PID 1a86:fe0c: Display FS V1 is FS35,
Display FS 0.96 Inch is FS096. Other products are listed as UNKNOWN.
Serial and manufacturer are optional. Multiple units are listed in tty-name order.
This is inventory, not permission to send commands or proof of hardware support.
No serial node is opened, no display commands are sent, and sudo is unnecessary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --verbose
Include sysfs, USB interface, driver and interface identifiers.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, including no devices; 1 on an incomplete scan or output error;
2 for invalid arguments. Missing optional fields appear as a dash.
Disconnected or stale links are skipped, with details in verbose mode.
